senses.gloss:
--the first of all धर्मस्;
1: वा. ८३. ६०.
hidden by कश्यप in a cave and discovered and published by Sanat- कुमार for the benefit of humanity;
2: Ib. ८३. ८३-4.
not to be discussed with Yogins; but implicit obedience to it leads to heaven, and non- conformity would lead to hell.
3: Ib. ८३. ९१-94; १०४. १४.

--of विष्णु on the waters: His primordial form;
1: भा. I. 3. 2-5.
his sleep at प्रयागा;
2: M. २२. 9.
left it for churning the ocean.
3: Ib. १५०. २१२; २४९. ४५.

--(Siddha) he who has practised brahmacarya, ahimsa, satya, non-stealing, and a parigraha and cultivated a sense of detachment;
1: वा. ७६. २८; Vi. VI. 7. ३६.
is superior to all for he performs तपस् for a hundred years standing on one foot and living on air;
2: वा. ७१. ७३.
धर्मशासनम् of: ahimsaka; walking on good roads, drinking clean and filtered water and speaking truthful words; after serving his guru for a year goes about begging alms;
3: Ib. १६. 8-१७.
gets the धारण and tries to avoid the उपसर्गस्; must understand the seven सूक्ष्मस्; महिसूक्ष्म, आप, तेजस्, वायु, व्योम, मनस् and बुद्धि सूक्ष्म, and the condition of these before these elements attain the स्थूलभाव; all of them inter-dependent;
4: Ib. १२. 9, १७.
always intent on प्राणायाम be- comes one with the great being;
5: Ib. १०. ९४.
the best to be fed on the occasion of the श्राद्ध; superior to the feeding of a thousand householders, a hundred वानप्रस्थस् and a thousand ब्रह्मचारिन्स्.
6: M. १३. 5; १६. १०; वा. ७१. ६७; Vi. III. १५. 2 and २४.
